                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really enjoy the Ty series. This isn't so much a, \"Hard no,\" and more a, \"Don't get your hopes up as you play.\"\n\nThe story is okay. Kind of weak overall, but it does enough for what the game is. [spoiler]The end of the game with Fluffy fell really flat for me. They tried to give her a redemption arc but it didn't work. Then the game ended real abruptly. Also, come to think of it, I don't think the guy we meet at the start of the game did anything besides stand by the gate.[/spoiler]\n\nThe main issue I have with this game is the lack of polish. I appreciate them trying new things, but the game feels rushed/had a limited budget. It crashed often, was buggy, and cutscenes glitched regularly (the most obvious being Ty's eyelids always clipping). \n\nThe game also has you backtracking a lot. A good hour or two could have been cut from my playthrough if I wasn't walking across the whole map for no reason. Especially since the game forces you slower in the open world compared to Ty 2, it's annoying.\n\nThere is a heavy focus on combat this game which isn't bad in itself. The gameplay can just get a bit repetitive.\n\nThe new 'rang system is a neat idea on paper. Who wouldn't want customizable, multi-purpose 'rangs? But the stones (which give your boomerangs their abilities) have zero description outside of the shops.* They also feel nerfed compared to previous, specialized 'rangs. I ended up just saving up for the end game boomerangs as quickly as I could and used those because the others were pointless. I'd rather have just had the specialized 'rangs that did their job well instead of these jack-of-all-trades.\n\nAlso, the cart racing.\nIt's bad.\nJust so, so bad to control.\nDemolition derbies can be cheesed by turning around. Items are not very self-explanatory on what they do.* Unlike Ty 2's cart racing, there's nothing redeeming about it.\n\n*These may have been intended to be reference in the manual in the original PS2 release.\n\n\nOverall, I don't hate the game. But I was pretty glad when it was over. Unless you're really invested in the franchise, you're fine skipping this one.",
